# Read by `vite build`, so a production build carries the API address without
# anything having to be configured in the hosting dashboard.
#
# This is here rather than only in Vercel's environment variables because a
# Vite build INLINES these values: a variable added in the dashboard changes
# nothing until someone redeploys, and a build that silently missed it
# produces a bundle that calls its own origin. That failure is quiet - the SPA
# fallback answers, so the login request gets a 200 with an HTML body instead
# of an error anyone can read.
#
# The API's root: no trailing slash, no /api/v1 - src/lib/api.ts appends that.
# A real environment variable still overrides this file, so Vercel's settings
# remain the way to point a preview build somewhere else.
#
# Not a secret. It is a public staging URL, and the browser sends it in every
# request anyway.
VITE_API_URL=https://staging.thirdeyegfx.in/nivisa
